From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: Run, LineBreak, Span -- a TextBlock's Inlines

NanaZip's About page sets its version in Runs of a TextBlock; there were no inlines and it crashed. Windows.UI.Xaml.Documents Run (Text), LineBreak and Span (Inlines), TextElement and Inline; TextBlock.Inlines (an InlineCollection: IVector<Inline>, IIDs from the type signatures). A TextBlock lays out its inlines' text when it has any -- runs one after the other, a line break as a new line -- and again when a run's Text changes. Markup: inline children of a TextBlock go to its Inlines; Run, LineBreak and Span elements; compiled Inlines collections. Per-run formatting comes later (runs take the TextBlock's). Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT); the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
